   "text": "Mokshit Sharma. Founding Engineer & Tech Lead at Movigo Innovations Pvt. Ltd. (Indore, India).\nI build intelligent systems, agentic workflows and data-driven products, and I measure them on held-out data before I trust them. I run the AI and data layer of a live delivery marketplace in Indore as its only engineer.\nEducation: Integrated B.Tech + M.Tech, Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, School of Data Science and Forecasting, Devi Ahilya Vishwavidyalaya, Indore, 2023 - 2028 (expected), CGPA 8.2.\nAvailability: Available for internships and full-time roles, remote, hybrid or on-site in India.\nEmail: mokshitsharmalaptop@gmail.com. GitHub: https://github.com/Mokshitsharma. LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/mokshit-sharma-75b5ab305/. Résumé: /resume/Mokshit_Sharma_Resume.pdf.\nPayPal AI Hackathon 2026: SettleAI entry; submissions close 12 November 2026, judging in December.\nEngineering principles: The model proposes, code decides. Agents draft plans, judgements and dispute splits. Deterministic code checks them before anything irreversible happens, and no agent holds a tool that can move money on its own. Exact checks run before the model. Photo timestamps, GPS distance, duplicate-image hashes and schema validation of a tool plan are cheap and certain, so they run first. The model only sees what rules cannot settle, and when the two disagree, the rule wins. A person approves the risky step. Approval is a step in the agent graph, not a line in a prompt. The run pauses, waits for a yes, and resumes without repeating tools that already ran. It runs without keys, and it is measured. Every external service has a mock and every model a stub, so tests and demos run offline. Evaluation checks whether the system is right, including whether it refuses when it should."
